{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}

[G]O come, all ye [D]faithful, [G]joyful and tri[D]umphant,
O [Em]come ye, O [D]come [A7]ye to [D]Bethlehem;
[G]Come and be[D]hold Him, [Em]born the [A7]King of [D]angels;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [D]come, let us a[G]dore Him,
O [C]come, let us a[G]dore [D]Him,
[G]Christ [C]the [D]Lord.

[G]Sing, choirs of [D]angels, [G]sing in exul[D]tation,
Sing, [Em]all ye [D]citi[A7]zens of [D]heaven above;
[G]Glory to [D]God, [Em]glory [A7]in the [D]highest;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [D]come, let us a[G]dore Him,
O [C]come, let us a[G]dore [D]Him,
[G]Christ [C]the [D]Lord.

[G]Yea, Lord, we [D]greet Thee, [G]born this happy [D]morning,
Je[Em]sus, to [D]Thee [A7]be [D]glory given;
[G]Word of the [D]Father, [Em]now in [A7]flesh ap[D]pearing;

{label: Chorus}
O [G]come, let us adore Him,
O [D]come, let us a[G]dore Him,
O [C]come, let us a[G]dore [D]Him,
[G]Christ [C]the [D]Lord.
